# Date (docs/date.md): a time value, whole milliseconds since 1970-01-01T00:00Z
# within 8.64e15 either way, or NaN for an invalid date, in UTC only. Every
# expected value was generated by Node 22 with TZ=UTC (diff-node runs with
# it too). A case named "deliberate" faults where JavaScript gives a value:
# what reads or writes local time (new Date with two or more arguments, a
# date and time string without Z or an offset, Date(), the local getters,
# toString and the like), the host's locale, a string JavaScript reads by its
# own heuristics, a conversion of an object (a coercion, ===, a set member),
# and the setters, which mutate (not built yet). Date.now() and new Date()
# read the host clock (@clock), as Temporal.Now does.

